LANGUAGES   += bash

# A tree that vendors this one aggregates it, and the aggregate's
# "make check" is a suite rather than every test in the build.  A
# suite collects nothing from a project that never named it --
# deliberately, because a project that has not heard of a suite has no
# opinion about which of its tests could run in it, and "all of them"
# is an opinion.  So this file has to say so, or every test below
# drops out of the aggregate's suites while a "make check" run in here
# still runs all of them and reports them green.  Which is exactly
# what was happening: the tests that guard pconfigure's own behaviour
# ran in neither of the GladeOS superproject's two suites, and the
# only place they ran was a "make check" nobody up there types.
#
# Being the tree a BOOTSTRAP names changes nothing about this, which
# is the part that made it easy to miss.  A bootstrap is an ordinary
# subproject in every way but the two it has to be special in -- a way
# to build a first pconfigure with none in hand, and a Makefile that
# says so -- so its tests reach a parent's suites by the same route as
# any other subproject's, and that route starts here.
#
# Both names rather than just smoke, and the reason is NOT that
# inclusion stops at a project boundary.  It used to be: a suite was
# told which tests an inclusion brought it by asking one project, so a
# subproject test that joined smoke did not arrive in a parent's
# overnight.  46df8ee ("pconfigure: Resolve an INCLUDE_TEST_SUITES
# across the whole build") ended that -- aggregate_test_suite_members
# unions every project's members and every project's includes first,
# then walks the inclusions once over the union -- so smoke alone here
# would in fact reach a parent's overnight that includes smoke.
#
# Both names anyway, because this project's membership should not
# depend on the parent's inclusion graph.  A parent that reorganises
# its suites, or vendors this tree into a build where overnight does
# not include smoke, would otherwise silently stop running these
# tests in it -- which is the failure this whole block exists to
# prevent, arriving by a different route.  Two lines is a cheap way
# not to care.
#
# And no DEFAULT_TEST_SUITE, so every TESTSRC below is a member of
# each of them without saying so, and a bare "make check" in here goes
# on meaning every test this project has.
TEST_SUITES += smoke
TEST_SUITES += overnight

